{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Stop the DVLA from passing on or selling a person's details to private companies",
        "additional_details": "Private parking companies often purchase drivers' details from the DVLA. They in turn can fine drivers for breaching parking rules in private car parks. The DVLA should not pass this information on to these companies as there is no legal requirement for them to so, nor should they sell it.",
        "background": "The DVLA is an executive agency of the Government that collates & stores vehicle and driver information. We want the Government to ban it from selling or passing on that information which it does not have a legal duty to provide.",
        "closed_at": null,
